GIVEN `P1, the amount of the employer's premium in 2011` IS A NUMBER
      `the person was required to pay an employer's premium in 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P2, the amount of the employer's premium in 2012` IS A NUMBER
      `the application is made in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the application is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `ei3 Refund`
DECIDE `s 96(8.91) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 2012` IS
    IF     `P1 as subsection (8.92) sets it` AT MOST 10_000
       AND `s 96(10) the application for the refund is made in time` `the application is made in writing to the Minister` 2012 `the day on which the application is made`
    THEN `ei3 the refund` (`ei3 the refund of` (`P2, the amount of the employer's premium in 2012` MINUS `P1 as subsection (8.92) sets it`) `if it is more than` 2)
             `capped at` 1_000
    ELSE `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
    WHERE
        `P1 as subsection (8.92) sets it` MEANS `s 96(8.92) P1 for subsection (8.91)` `P1, the amount of the employer's premium in 2011` `the person was required to pay an employer's premium in 2011`

-- Subsections (8.94) to (8.96): an employer's premium of $15,000 or less for 2012; the refund for 2013; P1 zero if none was required
-- for 2012, (8.95); at most $1,000, (8.96).
