§ `Section 96(11) to (13.1) - recovery, set-off, interest`

-- Subsection (11): if the Minister refunded, or applied to a liability to Her Majesty, more than should have been, "whether on
-- the basis of incorrect or incomplete information contained in the application or otherwise", the excess may be recovered at
-- any time from the person as a debt due to Her Majesty.
-- src:1605 | (11) If a person applies under this section for a refund and, whether on the basis of incorrect or incomplete information contained in the application or otherwise, the Minister has
-- src:1606 | (a) refunded an amount to the person, or
-- src:1607 | (b) applied an amount to a liability of the person to Her Majesty in right of Canada,
-- src:1608 | in excess of the amount that should have been refunded or applied, the excess amount may be recovered at any time from the person as a debt due to Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 96(11) (src:1605-1608)
GIVEN `the person applied under this section for a refund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount the Minister refunded to the person or applied to a liability of the person to Her Majesty` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that should have been refunded or applied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 96(11) the excess may be recovered at any time from the person as a debt due to Her Majesty` IF
        `the person applied under this section for a refund`
    AND `the amount the Minister refunded to the person or applied to a liability of the person to Her Majesty` GREATER THAN `the amount that should have been refunded or applied`

-- src:1605 | (11) If a person applies under this section for a refund and, whether on the basis of incorrect or incomplete information contained in the application or otherwise, the Minister has
-- src:1606 | (a) refunded an amount to the person, or
-- src:1607 | (b) applied an amount to a liability of the person to Her Majesty in right of Canada,
-- src:1608 | in excess of the amount that should have been refunded or applied, the excess amount may be recovered at any time from the person as a debt due to Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 96(11) (src:1605-1608)
GIVEN `the amount the Minister refunded to the person or applied to a liability of the person to Her Majesty` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that should have been refunded or applied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 96(11) the excess amount` IS
    IF `the amount the Minister refunded to the person or applied to a liability of the person to Her Majesty` GREATER THAN `the amount that should have been refunded or applied`
    THEN `the amount the Minister refunded to the person or applied to a liability of the person to Her Majesty` MINUS `the amount that should have been refunded or applied`
    ELSE 0

-- src:1610 | (12) If a person is liable or about to become liable to make a payment to Her Majesty in right of Canada and a refund under this section is otherwise payable to the person, the Minister may apply the amount of the refund to that liability and notify the person of that action instead of making the refund.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 96(12) (src:1610)
GIVEN `the person is liable or about to become liable to make a payment to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a refund under this section is otherwise payable to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 96(12) the Minister may apply the refund to that liability and notify the person instead of making the refund` IF
        `the person is liable or about to become liable to make a payment to Her Majesty in right of Canada`
    AND `a refund under this section is otherwise payable to the person`

-- Subsection (13.1): no interest on a refund payable under (3.1), (8.7), (8.91), (8.94), (8.97) or (8.98), nor on the amount of
-- such a refund applied to another liability.
DECLARE `ei3 Provision under which a refund is payable` IS ONE OF
    `ei3 subsection 96(1)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(2)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(3)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(3.1)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(4)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(5)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(5.1)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(6)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(7)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(8.2)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(8.3)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(8.7)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(8.91)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(8.94)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(8.97)`
    `ei3 subsection 96(8.98)`

-- src:1614 | (13.1) Despite subsection (13), no interest shall be paid on a refund payable under subsection (3.1), (8.7), (8.91), (8.94), (8.97) or (8.98) or on the amount of a refund payable under any of those subsections that is applied under this Act to any other liability.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 96(13.1) (src:1614)
GIVEN provision IS A `ei3 Provision under which a refund is payable`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 96(13.1) no interest shall be paid on the refund` IS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `ei3 subsection 96(3.1)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 subsection 96(8.7)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 subsection 96(8.91)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 subsection 96(8.94)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 subsection 96(8.97)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ei3 subsection 96(8.98)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Subsection (13): interest on an overpayment refunded, or applied to another liability, "at a prescribed annual rate ... for the
-- period or periods determined as prescribed", but none if the interest is less than $1. The rate and periods are prescribed
-- (Regulations not deposited), so the amount of interest is an input; the rule says whether it is paid.
-- src:1612 | (13) If an amount for an overpayment is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability, interest shall be paid or applied on the amount at a prescribed annual rate under the circumstances and for the period or periods determined as prescribed, except that no interest shall be paid or applied if the amount of the interest is less than $1.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 96(13) (src:1612)
GIVEN provision IS A `ei3 Provision under which a refund is payable`
      `an amount for an overpayment is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the interest at the prescribed annual rate for the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 96(13) interest shall be paid or applied on the amount` IF
        `an amount for an overpayment is refunded or applied under this Act to any other liability`
    AND (NOT `s 96(13.1) no interest shall be paid on the refund` provision)
    AND `the amount of the interest at the prescribed annual rate for the prescribed period` AT LEAST 1
